    "id": "pfe-whatwg-url",
    "prompt": "# Replace deprecated url.parse() with WHATWG URL API\n\n# Issue: Replace deprecated url.parse() with WHATWG URL API\n\n## Description\n\nThe library currently uses Node.js's deprecated `url.parse()` method, which triggers a DEP0169 deprecation warning in Node.js v14+:\n\n```\n(node:xxxxx) [DEP0169] DeprecationWarning: `url.parse()` behavior is not standardized and prone to errors that have security implications. Use the WHATWG URL API instead. CVEs are not issued for `url.parse()` vulnerabilities.\n```\n\nThis warning appears in projects that depend on `proxy-from-env` (directly or transitively through packages like axios).\n\n## Impact\n\n- **7.6 million+ dependent projects** are affected by this deprecation warning\n- The warning appears in popular packages:\n  - axios (used by millions of projects)\n  - Socket.io ([Issue #5377](https://github.com/socketio/socket.io/issues/5377))\n  - Microsoft Playwright ([Issue #38469](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/issues/38469))\n  - GitHub Actions setup-node ([Issue #1370](https://github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1370))\n  - Many Next.js applications\n  - And countless others\n\n## Current Code\n\n```javascript\n// Line 3\nvar parseUrl = require('url').parse;\n\n// Line 24\nvar parsedUrl = typeof url === 'string' ? parseUrl(url) : url || {};\n```\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\nReplace `url.parse()` with the WHATWG URL API (`new URL()`):\n\n```javascript\nfunction parseUrl(urlString) {\n  try {\n    return new URL(urlString);\n  } catch (error) {\n    // Return empty object for invalid URLs (matching url.parse behavior)\n    return {};\n  }\n}\n\nvar parsedUrl = typeof url === 'string' ? parseUrl(url) : url || {};\n```\n\n## Benefits\n\n1. ✅ Eliminates deprecation warning\n2. ✅ Uses standardized WHATWG URL API\n3. ✅ Maintains backward compatibility\n4. ✅ Same behavior for invalid URLs\n5. ✅ Future-proof (Node.js may eventually remove `url.parse()`)\n\n## Compatibility\n\n- The WHATWG URL API has been available since Node.js v7.0.0 (2016)\n- Current proxy-from-env requires Node.js >=6.0.0\n- The library only uses 3 properties: `protocol`, `host`, and `port`\n- These properties exist on both `url.parse()` results and WHATWG `URL` objects\n\n## Testing\n\nThe fix has been tested with:\n- Valid HTTP/HTTPS URLs\n- Invalid URLs (returns empty object)\n- URLs with various proxy environment variable configurations\n- Both string URLs and pre-parsed URL objects\n\n## Additional Context\n\nNode.js documentation states:\n> The legacy `url.parse()` API is deprecated. Users should use the WHATWG URL API instead. CVEs are not issued for `url.parse()` \n...(issue 正文已截断)\n\n---\n以上是 Rob--W/proxy-from-env 仓库的真实 issue（#32）。请在该仓库中修复它。\n要求：不要修改任何测试文件；改完后运行测试确认通过。",
